          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/29",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s172",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "וַיֹּ֣אמֶר אֲבִימֶ֖לֶךְ אֶל־אַבְרָהָ֑ם מָ֣ה הֵ֗נָּה שֶׁ֤בַע כְּבָשֹׂת֙ הָאֵ֔לֶּה אֲשֶׁ֥ר הִצַּ֖בְתָּ לְבַדָּֽנָה׃"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/30",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s172",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "וַיֹּ֗אמֶר כִּ֚י אֶת־שֶׁ֣בַע כְּבָשֹׂ֔ת תִּקַּ֖ח מִיָּדִ֑י בַּעֲבוּר֙ תִּֽהְיֶה־לִּ֣י לְעֵדָ֔ה כִּ֥י חָפַ֖רְתִּי אֶת־הַבְּאֵ֥ר הַזֹּֽאת׃"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/31",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s172",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "עַל־כֵּ֗ן קָרָ֛א לַמָּק֥וֹם הַה֖וּא בְּאֵ֣ר שָׁ֑בַע כִּ֛י שָׁ֥ם נִשְׁבְּע֖וּ שְׁנֵיהֶֽם׃"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/32",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s172",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "וַיִּכְרְת֥וּ בְרִ֖ית בִּבְאֵ֣ר שָׁ֑בַע וַיָּ֣קָם אֲבִימֶ֗לֶךְ וּפִיכֹל֙ שַׂר־צְבָא֔וֹ וַיָּשֻׁ֖בוּ אֶל־אֶ֥רֶץ פְּלִשְׁתִּֽים׃"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/33",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s172",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "וַיִּטַּ֥ע אֶ֖שֶׁל בִּבְאֵ֣ר שָׁ֑בַע וַיִּ֨קְרָא־שָׁ֔ם בְּשֵׁ֖ם יְהוָ֥ה אֵ֥ל עוֹלָֽם׃"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/34",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s172",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "וַיָּ֧גָר אַבְרָהָ֛ם בְּאֶ֥רֶץ פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים יָמִ֥ים רַבִּֽים׃"
              }
            ],
            "end_reference": true
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s172",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "instructions": [
              {
                "text": "פ",
                "type": "description",
                "language": "he"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "en": [
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/1",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s169",
                "printed_page": "73",
                "text": "The Lord considered Sarah just as He had said and the Lord did for Sarah just as He had spoken."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/2",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s169",
                "printed_page": "73",
                "text": "And Sarah conceived and bore a son to Abraham in his old age at the appointed time which God had told him."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/3",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s169",
                "printed_page": "73",
                "text": "Abraham called the name of his son, who was born to him, whom Sarah had born to him, Isaac."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/4",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s169",
                "printed_page": "73",
                "text": "Abraham circumcised his son Isaac when he was eight days old just as God had commanded him."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/5",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s169",
                "printed_page": "73",
                "text": "Abraham was a hundred years old, when his son Isaac was born to him."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/6",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s169",
                "printed_page": "73",
                "text": "Then Sarah said: ‘God has given me mirth; everyone who hears of it will laugh with me’."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/7",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s169",
                "printed_page": "73",
                "text": "She said: ‘Who would have foretold to Abraham that Sarah would suckle children; yet have I born him a son in his old age’."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/8",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s169",
                "printed_page": "73",
                "text": "The child grew and was weaned; and Abraham prepared a great feast on the day Isaac was weaned."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/9",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s169",
                "printed_page": "73",
                "text": "Then Sarah saw the son of Hagar the Egyptian"
              },
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "woman, whom she had born to Abraham, scoffing."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/10",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "So she said to Abraham: ‘Drive away this slave-girl and her son, for the son of this slave-girl shall not inherit together with my son, Isaac’."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/11",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "And this thing seemed very wrong in Abraham’s eyes because of his son."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/12",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "Then God said to Abraham: ‘Let it not seem wrong in your eyes concerning the lad and your slave-girl. With regard to all that Sarah tells you, listen to her voice, for it is through Isaac that descendants will be called after you."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/13",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "And also the son of the slave-girl will I make a nation because he too is your seed’."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/14",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "Then Abraham rose early in the morning and took a loaf of bread and a water-skin and gave them to Hagar, placing them upon her shoulder, as well as the child and sent her away. She went and roamed about in the wilderness of Beersheba."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/15",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "When the water in the skin came to an end she put the child under one of the bushes."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/16",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "Then she went away and sat down at a distance of a bow shot because she thought: ‘Let me not see the child die’. She sat down at a distance and raised her voice and wept."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/17",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "And God heard the lad’s voice and an angel of God called to Hagar from heaven and said to her: ‘What troubles you, Hagar? Do not be afraid. God has heard the lad’s voice from where he is."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/18",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "Rise, lift up the lad and hold him firmly with the hand, for I will make him a great nation’."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/19",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "And God opened her eyes and she saw a well of water and she went and filled the skin with water and gave the lad to drink."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/20",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "And God was with the lad and he grew up and lived in the wilderness and became an archer."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/21",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "He lived in the wilderness of Paran and his mother took a wife for him from the land of Egypt."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/22",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "It was at that time that Abimelekh and Pikhol, the general of his army, spoke to Abraham saying: ‘God is with you in everything that you do."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/23",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s171",
                "printed_page": "74",
                "text": "So now swear to me here by God that you will not be untrue"
              },
              {
                "scan": "s173",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "to me or to my son or my grandson; according to the kindness that I have shown you, so may you show me kindness as well as the land in which you have resided’."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/24",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s173",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "And Abraham said: ‘I swear’."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/25",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s173",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "Then Abraham remonstrated with Abimelekh about the well of water which the servants of Abimelekh had stolen."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/26",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s173",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "Abimelekh said: ‘I do not know who has done this; you did not tell me about it, nor have I heard about it until today’."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/27",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s173",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "Then Abraham took sheep and cattle and gave them to Abimelekh and they both concluded a covenant."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/28",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s173",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "Abraham set apart seven lambs."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/29",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s173",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "Then Abimelekh said to Abraham: ‘What is the meaning of these seven lambs which you have set apart?’"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/30",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s173",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "He said: ‘Take these seven lambs from my hand so that these may be evidence for me that I dug this well’."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/31",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s173",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "Therefore that place was called Beersheba because both of them took an oath there."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/32",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s173",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "And they concluded a covenant in Beersheba. And Abimelekh arose together with Pikhol, the general of his army and they returned to the land of the Philistines."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/33",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s173",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "And Abraham planted a tree in Beersheba and there He called on the Name of the Lord, the God of eternity."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "paragraph": 1,
            "corresp": "urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:genesis/21/34",
            "fragments": [
              {
                "scan": "s173",
                "printed_page": "75",
                "text": "And Abraham resided in the land of the Philistines for many days."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
